//  Day 2 HTML form
Form is box to all input element

<form>
<input type="text">
</form>

withput <form>, browser don't know this is form.

<input> for receive input from user.
<input type="text">


*input attribute:

-text, for short text like name, city, and more.

-number, for number like age.

-email, for email.

-password, for password. the input can;t be seen (••••••••). (it's only the view, not make sure your password secure).

-date, for date. (will show calendar).

-checkbox, for many option like exam. 
<input type="checkbox"> HTML
<input type="checkbox"> CSS
<input type="checkbox"> JavaScript

-radio, same like checkbox, but user can only pick one. 
**for related radio, must use the same name:

<input type="radio" name="gender">
<input type="radio" name="gender">

if not, user can pick both at the same time.




====================================
**name
name is data name that will send to the server.
example : <input type="text" name="username">

in PHP $_POST['username']

**placeholder
guidance for the user. example:
<input type="email" placeholder="Masukkan email">

**label
for the input label. example:
<label for="email">Email</label>
<input type="email" id="email">

**relationship betwee for and id in label and input

<label for="username">
<input id="username">

if the user click label name, then input will focus.

-textarea, for long text like opinion.

-select and option, for choice.
<select> //box
    <option>Bandung</option> // 3 choice
    <option>Jakarta</option>
    <option>Bogor</option>
</select>

-required, must fill attribute.
<input type="text" required>
if null, browser will decline submit.

-value, first value of input.
<input type="text" value="Budi">

<input type="radio"
       name="gender"
       value="L">